10|The Almost-Perfect Picnic|差一点完美的野餐|周末与朋友|野餐快开始时才发现没带餐具，朋友们一起想办法。|检查准备、说明遗漏、调整计划
picnic=野餐|fork=叉子|spread out=铺开
Did anyone bring forks?|I thought you had them.|We can still make this work.
lucy: Little Moments. The Almost-Perfect Picnic. Emma and I spread out a blanket in the park. Mom sets down the cooler, and Ben arrives carrying a bag of chips like it's a precious treasure. The weather is perfect. The food looks great. Then I open the pasta salad.
emma: Did anyone bring forks?
lucy: I thought you had them.
emma: I brought plates. You said you were bringing the other stuff.
ben: I brought chips. I did my job beautifully.
mom: Let's see what we have before we go anywhere. Sandwiches, fruit, crackers, and that pasta salad.
lucy: We can still make this work. We eat the sandwiches first. Emma passes around the fruit, and Ben opens his very important bag of chips. Nobody seems unhappy.
emma: The pasta can come home with us. It'll be an excellent second picnic on the kitchen table.
mom: Good plan. I'll keep it cold in the cooler until we get home.
lucy: We watch a tiny dog trying to carry a stick twice its size. Ben puts a cracker next to his sandwich and says he's building a food castle.
emma: Next time, let's make one list and put our names beside the things we're bringing.
ben: Put me down for chips again. I'm experienced now.
lucy: On the way home, I add forks to our next picnic list. Then I add a second line underneath: Check that someone actually packed the forks. That feels like an important detail.
===
11|The Red Sock Mystery|红袜子去了哪里|家庭日常|整理衣服时总有袜子失踪，Lucy和Ben展开调查。|配对、描述位置、分配家务
laundry=洗好的衣物|pair=一双|inside out=里外翻面的
These two don't match.|Turn it inside out.|Can you help me fold these, Ben?
lucy: Little Moments. The Red Sock Mystery. Saturday morning, Mom drops a basket of clean laundry on the couch. It's warm, fluffy, and much taller than it looked in the dryer. Can you help me fold these, Ben?
ben: Only if I can be in charge of socks. I'm very good at socks.
lucy: Five minutes later, he hands me a red sock and a striped sock. These two don't match.
ben: They both fit on feet. That's something.
mom: There should be another red one somewhere. Check the bigger clothes before we blame the washing machine.
lucy: We shake out a towel. Nothing. We check a pillowcase. Still nothing. Ben holds up Dad's sweatshirt and makes it dance.
ben: Maybe the sock moved away. Maybe it wanted a bigger closet.
lucy: Wait. There's a little lump in that sleeve. Turn it inside out.
ben: Aha! One red sock, hiding from its responsibilities.
lucy: We put the pair together and finish the basket. I fold shirts while Ben matches the rest of the socks. This time, he checks the colors and patterns.
mom: Nice work. You two make a good team.
ben: Do good teams get a snack break?
lucy: Mom points toward the kitchen. Ben races off, then comes back holding one striped sock.
ben: Small problem. This one is alone now.
lucy: I look at the empty basket. The mystery is not over. Our snack break, however, is absolutely still happening.
===
12|Can I Try Another Size?|能换个尺码试试吗|吃饭与购物|试鞋时Lucy发现好看不等于合脚。|询问尺码、试穿、描述舒适度
size=尺码|tight=紧的|heel=脚跟
Can I try another size?|These feel a little tight.|Take a few steps.
lucy: Little Moments. Can I Try Another Size? Dad takes me shopping for new sneakers because my old ones are getting tight. At the store, I find a purple pair with bright yellow laces. They're exactly the colors I wanted.
clerk: What size do you usually wear?
lucy: A six, I think. The clerk brings a box, and I sit down to try them on. They look amazing. My toes do not seem as excited as I am.
dad: How do they feel?
lucy: These feel a little tight. Maybe they'll be okay if I don't move much.
dad: That could be a problem for shoes.
clerk: We can try half a size up. You should be able to walk comfortably.
lucy: Can I try another size? The clerk brings the bigger pair, and I put both shoes on this time.
clerk: Take a few steps. See if your heel stays in place and your toes have room.
lucy: I walk toward the mirror and back. Much better. I can actually imagine running for the bus in these.
dad: Hopefully, we'll leave early enough that you won't need to.
lucy: At the counter, the clerk asks if I want to wear them out of the store. I say yes and put my old shoes in the box.
dad: Ready?
lucy: More than ready. I take one big, comfortable step. The yellow laces bounce. My toes and I have finally agreed on something.
===
13|You Got My Name Almost Right|名字差一点就对了|吃饭与购物|取餐单把Lucy写成了Lucky，引出轻松的小对话。|报名字、拼写、确认订单
spell=拼写|order=订单|pickup=取餐
Could you spell that for me?|I think that's my order.|Close enough.
lucy: Little Moments. You Got My Name Almost Right. Emma and I order sandwiches at a busy cafe. The person at the register asks for my name, but the coffee machine starts making a loud noise just as I answer.
clerk: Sorry, what was that?
lucy: Lucy.
clerk: Got it. Two sandwiches. We'll call you when they're ready.
lucy: We find a table near the pickup counter. Emma takes off her jacket, and I watch people walk past the window. A minute later, someone calls out a name I don't recognize.
clerk: Lucky! Order for Lucky!
emma: Are we lucky today? Because those look a lot like our sandwiches.
lucy: I walk over and check the bag. One cheese sandwich, one turkey sandwich. I think that's my order.
clerk: Lucky?
lucy: Lucy, actually. Close enough.
clerk: Oh, sorry about that. Could you spell that for me?
lucy: L, U, C, Y. The clerk corrects the name on the receipt and gives me the bag. I thank her and bring lunch to our table.
emma: Congratulations on your new name. Does it come with extra cookies?
lucy: Apparently not. I check the bag just in case. Only sandwiches and napkins. But my sandwich has an especially big slice of cheese, so maybe I am lucky.
emma: Next time, I'll order under my name.
lucy: Good idea. Let's see if you become Emily, Emma, or Excellent. I think Excellent would suit you for at least one lunch.
===
14|The Homework Help Call|一起弄懂作业要求|校园生活|Lucy和Emma通话核对作业，发现自己看错了页码。|请求解释、澄清要求、核对信息
instructions=说明|page=页码|explain=解释
Could you explain that again?|Which page are you on?|That makes more sense.
lucy: Little Moments. The Homework Help Call. I'm staring at my notebook when Emma calls. She's already finished our English assignment. I have written exactly one word, and that word is my name.
emma: How's it going?
lucy: Slowly. I don't understand why we need to write about a jungle. Our class was talking about neighborhoods today.
emma: A jungle? Which page are you on?
lucy: Thirty-eight. The instructions say to describe an adventure. I was about to put a tiger next to the grocery store.
emma: We're on page eighty-three. Describe your neighborhood, then add one place you'd like to have nearby.
lucy: I turn the pages. There it is. That makes more sense. Could you explain that again? Just the part about the new place.
emma: Write about a real place first. Then imagine something useful or fun, like a swimming pool or a bigger park. The rest is your choice.
lucy: Thanks. What did you pick?
emma: A library with comfortable reading chairs. But you should choose something you actually want.
lucy: I look out my window at the empty lot down the street. I would love a little basketball court there. I start writing before the idea disappears.
emma: All set now?
lucy: I think so. No more jungle.
emma: You can save the tiger for another assignment.
lucy: I write the page number at the top of my notebook. Eighty-three. I check it twice. My neighborhood already feels much safer without that tiger beside the vegetables.
===
15|Who Turned Off the Wi-Fi?|家里的网络掉线了|家庭日常|视频突然停住，一家人一起找出简单原因。|描述问题、确认连接、请求等待
frozen=画面卡住的|plug=插头|connection=连接
The screen is frozen.|Is it working for you?|Give it a minute.
lucy: Little Moments. Who Turned Off the Wi-Fi? Emma and I are on a video call, planning our class poster. She holds up a sketch, opens her mouth, and turns into a statue. The screen is frozen. Emma? Can you hear me?
ben: If she's doing a robot impression, it's really good.
lucy: My phone says there's no connection. Is it working for you? Ben checks his tablet and shakes his head. We call Dad, who is putting away the vacuum cleaner.
dad: Let me have a look. Did it stop just now?
lucy: About a minute ago. Dad follows the cable from the router to the wall. The plug is hanging loose beside the outlet.
dad: That would explain it. I must have unplugged it when I moved the vacuum. My mistake.
ben: So the internet wasn't broken. It was just taking a nap.
dad: Something like that. I'll plug it back in. Give it a minute.
lucy: We wait while the little lights come back on. I open our call again, and Emma finally starts moving.
emma: There you are! Did you see my drawing?
lucy: Only the first half. You looked very serious for a while.
emma: That's my thinking face.
lucy: We finish planning on paper, then take photos to share. Dad promises to check the plugs next time he cleans. Ben promises to tell everyone he personally watched the internet wake up. Somehow, that becomes the biggest news of the afternoon.
===
16|Two Tickets, Please|买两张电影票|周末与朋友|选座、买票和找影厅，Lucy第一次认真参与安排。|选择座位、确认时间、询问位置
ticket=票|row=排|middle=中间
Two tickets, please.|Are there seats near the middle?|Which way is theater three?
lucy: Little Moments. Two Tickets, Please. Dad and I arrive at the movie theater twenty minutes early. I have one job today: help choose the seats. Dad says this is more important than choosing the popcorn. I am not completely convinced.
clerk: Hi there. What would you like to see?
lucy: The animated movie at two thirty. Two tickets, please.
clerk: Sure. Here's the seating chart. The gray seats are taken, and the blue ones are available.
lucy: Are there seats near the middle?
clerk: Row six has two together. Or you can sit closer to the front in row three.
dad: Row six sounds good to me. What do you think?
lucy: Perfect. I don't want to spend the whole movie looking straight up. We get our tickets and move away from the counter. Then I realize I forgot to ask one thing. Which way is theater three?
clerk: Down the hall on your left, just past the restrooms.
lucy: Thanks. We find our seats with plenty of time. I check the numbers twice before we sit down.
dad: Excellent planning. Now, about that popcorn.
lucy: I knew it was important. We share a small bag and watch the screen fill with trailers. Before the movie starts, Dad silences his phone, and I do the same.
dad: Ready for the adventure?
lucy: Yes. Middle seats, snacks, and no neck pain. I think my first day as the family seat expert is going pretty well.
===
17|The Tiny Birthday Secret|小小的生日秘密|周末与朋友|Lucy和Emma准备惊喜卡片，Ben努力保守秘密。|邀请帮忙、约定时间、保守惊喜
surprise=惊喜|card=卡片|secret=秘密
Don't tell her yet.|What time should I come over?|I'll keep it a secret.
lucy: Little Moments. The Tiny Birthday Secret. Mom's birthday is tomorrow. Emma has offered to help me make a big card, and Ben has offered to help by asking a lot of questions. I call Emma after dinner.
emma: What time should I come over?
lucy: Ten tomorrow morning. Dad's taking Mom out for breakfast. We'll have about an hour to finish the card and set the table.
ben: Are we having cake? Is the cake a secret? Can I taste the secret?
lucy: Everything is a secret until Mom gets home. Don't tell her yet.
ben: I'll keep it a secret. I am excellent at not talking.
lucy: He proves this by talking for another five minutes. The next morning, Emma arrives with colored paper and stickers. We write little messages inside the card. Mine says thank you for helping me even when I'm grumpy.
emma: That's a good message. Mine says happy birthday to the best pancake maker I know.
ben: Mine says I love you more than cake. Is that believable?
lucy: Very generous of you. We hear the front door, so we hide the card behind our backs. Mom walks into the kitchen and stops.
mom: Why is everybody standing so strangely?
ben: No reason. Definitely not because of a giant card.
lucy: We all laugh and hold it up. Surprise! Mom reads every message slowly. Then she hugs us, including our terrible little secret keeper. The card is slightly crooked, but her smile is perfect.
